-- title:
--   Galois-compatible generic fibre from the chart-ring identifications
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$, a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} =$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) $\ell$ for the subring of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, and $F_N =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull` $N$ for the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the divisor expansions of level $N$. Let $\bar{j} =$ `jBar` $N$ be the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion of $j$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \otimes$-base change $\bar{F}_N =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar` $N \subset \overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$. Assume $\bar{j}$ is transcendental over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, that $\bar{j} \neq 0$, and that $\bar{F}_N$ is finite-dimensional both over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(\bar{j})$ and over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(\bar{j}^{-1})$ (the intermediate fields generated by $\{\bar{j}\}$, resp. $\{\bar{j}^{-1}\}$). Assume given two $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra isomorphisms: $e_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}}$ `chartAlgFin` $N\,\ell$ onto the ring of elements of $\bar{F}_N$ integral over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}[\bar{j}]$, and $e_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}}$ `chartAlgInf` $N\,\ell$ onto the elements integral over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}[\bar{j}^{-1}]$, each sending $1 \otimes b$ to the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb` of the Laurent series $b \in F_N$. Let $M_\eta =$ `CurveModel.ofGenerator` $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,\bar{j}$ be the curve model of $\bar{F}_N$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ attached to the transcendental generator $\bar{j}$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a morphism $e_\eta$ from $M_\eta.C$ to the pullback of `igusaTo` $N\,\ell$ along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, together with the assertion that $e_\eta$ is an isomorphism, such that: (i) $e_\eta$ followed by the second pullback projection equals $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$; and (ii) for every $g \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ and any two $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, x'$ of $M_\eta.C$ (sections of $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$), if the image of $x'$ in the Igusa scheme under $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(g)$ followed by the corresponding image of $x$, then $M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x' = \mathrm{arithmeticGalois}\,F_N\,g \cdot M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x$, the action being that of the semilinear automorphism attached to $g$ on places of $\bar{F}_N$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   This is the step that converts the two chart-level algebra identifications into an identification of the curve model of the modular function field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(X_0(N))$ generated by $j$ with the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the Igusa scheme over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$, in a way that matches conjugation of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points by $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ with the arithmetic Galois action on places. It is used by [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_genericFibre_iso_ofGenerator_jBar_and_galoisCompat`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_genericFibre_iso_ofGenerator_jBar_and_galoisCompat), where the hypotheses $e_{\mathrm{Fin}}$, $e_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ are supplied from the chart-ring comparison.
